ng a twin"},{"label":"C","text":"Maize based diet with little milk"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"07ae837d55b90848ef141bdac51cf11f620a387f"},{"id":"q-77c53844bd92","stem":"Which of the following laboratory values is normally higher in childhood than in adulthood?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Labor and Delivery","options":[{"label":"A","text":"hemoglobin concentration"},{"label":"B","text":"serum alkaline phosphatase"},{"label":"C","text":"serum cholesterol"},{"label":"D","text":"serum sodium"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d9f22af3314b831c8b9e8c5002a6b9d81aa13576"},{"id":"q-abf6709bb5a4","stem":"Most infants lose weight immediately after birth. Normal, term infants generally regain their birth weight by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"48 hours"},{"label":"B","text":"72 hours"},{"label":"C","text":"3 to 5 days"},{"label":"D","text":"7 to 10 days"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7d6421a3d12e","stem":". The anterior fontanel usually feels closed on physical examination (palpation)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"between 3 and 9 months"},{"label":"B","text":"between 9 and 18 months"},{"label":"C","text":"between 18 and 24 months"},{"label":"D","text":"between 24 and 36 months"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-90ceba0e7f22","stem":". A premature infants is delivered precipitously and appears asphyxiated. The infant is cyanotic, there are no respiratory efforts, and the heart rate is 80 per minute. The infant is stained with thick meconium, and meconium is noted in the amniotic fluid and in the infant’ s mouth. At this point you should","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"start bag-and-mask ventilation with 100% oxygen"},{"label":"B","text":"suction the oropharynx and trachea through an endotracheal tube to remove the meconium, then ventilate"},{"label":"C","text":"suction the oropharynx, then start bag- and mask ventilation"},{"label":"D","text":"establish monitoring with ECG and pulse oximeter"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-21b001d9038e","stem":"The major route for excretion of bilirubin in the fetus in utero is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"via the kidney"},{"label":"B","text":"transplacental passage"},{"label":"C","text":"degradation to biliverdin"},{"label":"D","text":"hepatic secretion and storage in the intestinal lumen"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c9e07784fd7f","stem":"Kernicterus is most closely related to the serum level of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"total bilirubin"},{"label":"B","text":"conjugated bilirubin"},{"label":"C","text":"unconjugated bilirubin"},{"label":"D","text":"haptoglobin"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f0209aef86b2c2a2850f7342d6ad0bf831f84ba6"},{"id":"q-ec9140683a40","stem":"The following congenital abnormalities are deformations, not malformations","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Talipes"},{"label":"B","text":"Congenital heart defect"},{"label":"C","text":"Polydaktyly"},{"label":"D","text":"Renal agenesis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-cdfbf5a5511f","stem":"The following conditions are inherited as sex- linked recessive traits","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sickle cell disease"},{"label":"B","text":"Duchenne muscular dystrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Osteogenesis imperfecta"},{"label":"D","text":"Turner Syndrome"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3c49aefe8fea","stem":"Brain tumors in children","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"may present with seizures"},{"label":"B","text":"do not lead to symptoms of raised intracranial pressure because of the distensibility of the skull in childhood"},{"label":"C","text":"are frequently metastases from extra cranial tumors"},{"label":"D","text":"do not require treatment if the histology is benign"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6cd60b36dab2","stem":". In the assessment and management of epilepsy in childhood","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"a normal EEG will exclude the diagnosis in a doubtful case"},{"label":"B","text":"intramuscular diazepam is more effective than rectal diazepam in the treatment of status epilepticus"},{"label":"C","text":"Sodium Valproate has been associated with acute liver failure"},{"label":"D","text":"Phenytoin is the drug of first choice for all types of epilepsy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-be6faa6c8e53","stem":"An infant born at 39 weeks of gestation and weighing 2000g should be classified as","type":"OSCE / Practical Station","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Low birth weight and small for gestational age"},{"label":"B","text":"Low birth weight"},{"label":"C","text":"Small for gestational age"},{"label":"D","text":"premature and small for gestational age"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"f54e73489f287bcf1a65a61307cd4889031351b4"},{"id":"q-670986624244","stem":"In the Tanzanian Vaccination Schedule the live attenuated measles vaccine should be administered","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"at 6 months"},{"label":"B","text":"at 9 months"},{"label":"C","text":"at 15 months"},{"label":"D","text":"at 24 months SAQ"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"ee5686f6fe454f80aa8472c7861a1291d418d093"},{"id":"q-c825d13ef3df","stem":"TRUE/FALSE QUESTIONS (1) Which criteria have to be fulfilled to call a convulsion an “ uncomplicated febrile convulsion “ ? (a)...it has to occur between the age of 5-6 months to 5-6 years- TRUE (b) it has to be associated with urinary incontinence- True (c) duration at least 20 minutes- FALSE (d) it has to be generalized- (e) the focus of infection has to be outside the CNS-TRUE (max. 5 marks) (2) Complications of Kwashiorkor are (a) Staphylococcal Sepsis-TRUE (b) Pneumonia-TRUE (c) Hypoglycemia-TRUE (d) anuria-TRUE (e) cardiac arrhythmias-TRUE (max. 5 marks) (3) A typical Nephrotic Syndrome is characterized by the following: (a) low Serum Protein-TRUE (b) Hyperkalemia-FALSE (c) Hypercholesterinemia-TRUE (d) Edema-TRUE (e) high Blood pressure-FALSE (max. 5 marks) (4) Iron deficiency anemia is characterized by (a) reduced mean corpuscular volume (MCV)-TRUE (b) increased MCV-FALSE (c) megaloblasts in periphery-FALSE (d) easy fatiguability-TRUE (e) hypochromic red blood cells-TRUE (max. 5 marks) (5) A 1 year old child is brought with a 2 day history of pain in the left leg. Examination reveals a miserable child with bony tenderness over the upper end of the left tibia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"A normal X-Ray will exclude osteomyelitis / osteitis-FALSE"},{"label":"B","text":"If a diagnosis of osteomyelitis is made antibiotic treatment should be postponed until the result of blood culture is obtained-FALSE"},{"label":"C","text":"If early osteomyelitis is confirmed the treatment of choice is orthopedic intervention and parenteral antibiotics-TRUE"},{"label":"D","text":"Ultrasound may reveal subperiostal fluid accumulation-TRUE (max. 4 marks)"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["possible_multiple_questions_in_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-b61111b1aeb9