"auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-5090dafc8af5","stem":"How can you prevent Rickets in the preterm child and at what age does the preventive treatment start?","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e707ca993ccd","stem":"Name findings which you will be looking for during your clinical examination .................................................... ( 2 marks) Question 13 + 14: A 3 year old child presents with a history of cough for 3 months, loss of weight and loss of appetite. On examination you find an underweight child, no generalized lymphadenopathy, respiratory rate of 36/min, no chest indrawings and bronchial breathing over the right upper zone. The temperature is 37.2 degree Celsius.","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-7b9201fa407c","stem":"Name 2 investigations you would order first....................................(2 marks)","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"