ion last week) until 6 hours ago, when he suddenly began screaming every 10 minutes. He is afebrile; he vomited twice but has no diarrhea, although he clearly has cramping abdominal pain. On physical examination you feel a mass in the right upper quadrant. You find bloody stool in the rectum.","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-80673097b6ff","stem":"Match the following seizure descriptions with the commonly used classification of seizures by the International League against epilepsy (ILAE) ( 6 marks) List 1","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"focal motor or sensory signs without impairment of consciousness-3"},{"label":"B","text":"sudden blank staring for some seconds, sometimes associated with eye-lid blinking- 2"},{"label":"C","text":"aura, followed by twitching of one side of the body without loss of consciousness-1"},{"label":"D","text":"focal motor, sensory or autonomic signs associated with impairment of consciousness- 1"},{"label":"E","text":"aura followed by twitching of the whole body and loss of consciousness-4"},{"label":"F","text":"sudden onset of twitching of the whole body with loss of consciousness-2 List 2:"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAud