pace posterior axillary line"},{"label":"B","text":"Is inserted at the inferior angle of the scapula"},{"label":"C","text":"For pneumothorax is inserted at 3rd intercostals space anteriorly"},{"label":"D","text":"May be inserted using trocar and cannula"},{"label":"E","text":"There is only one method of inserting the tube"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8665de009bd1","stem":"The following are true above chest tube insertion","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is done just below the rib above in the intercostals space"},{"label":"B","text":"5% lignocaine is used as local anaesthetic"},{"label":"C","text":"For haemothorax is inserted in 7th intercostals space in the midaxillary line"},{"label":"D","text":"For Empyema thracis is inserted in the 2nd intercostals space midaxillary line"},{"label":"E","text":"1% xylocane may be used"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-04af28c4c660","stem":"The following are true about pneumothorax except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"May be spontaneous or following trauma"},{"label":"B","text":"Is associated with sudden chest pain"},{"label":"C","text":"Is characterized by hyperresonance"},{"label":"D","text":"May be associated with ventilatory and circulatory compromise"},{"label":"E","text":"If it is less than 25% will need tube thoracostomy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-702e650abf86","stem":"Before inserting a chest tube the skin is prepared as follows","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cetrimide cleaning followed by providone painting"},{"label":"B","text":"Cleaning with methylated spirit"},{"label":"C","text":"Povidone iodine paint"},{"label":"D","text":"SSD cream application"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-be32d0bfe7d6","stem":"The following items can be sterilized using chemical method","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Surgical linen"},{"label":"B","text":"Esophagascope"},{"label":"C","text":"Dressing gauze"},{"label":"D","text":"Laryngascope"},{"label":"E","text":"‘b’ and ‘d’"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8b76dba4d9f6","stem":"The following method of sterilization is used in industries for Mass production of sterile medical products","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chemical"},{"label":"B","text":"Autoclaving"},{"label":"C","text":"Gamma radiation"},{"label":"D","text":"Hot air oven"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above 3"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f96235ac2eb1d4599b08794100cd3e77cac22e39"},{"id":"q-6a335a0b70bb","stem":"Shock is defined as the circumstance of insufficient oxygen delivery to the tissues. Etiology of shock in surgical patients is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Emergency Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vomiting"},{"label":"B","text":"Dirrhoea"},{"label":"C","text":"Burn injury"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above except (b)"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Emergency Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5a9167c1ddcf","stem":"Haemorhagic shock consists of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Emergency Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hypovolemia"},{"label":"B","text":"Inadequate venous return (cardiac filling pressure)"},{"label":"C","text":"Hemodilution of Hb with low O2 carrying capacity"},{"label":"D","text":"Depressed cariac out put"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Emergency Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b4e0e95663de","stem":"Hypovolemic shock can be seen in patients with the following conditions except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Emergency Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Intestinal obstruction low and high"},{"label":"B","text":"Burn injury > 30%"},{"label":"C","text":"Excessive sweating"},{"label":"D","text":"Ruptured visceral"},{"label":"E","text":"Moderate Head injury"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Emergency Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e7d5d7d403fa","stem":"One of the following sentences is not correct","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sterilization is the destruction all living microbes"},{"label":"B","text":"Disinfection is the removal of harmful microbes not usually including bacterial spores"},{"label":"C","text":"Sterilized equipment is essential for all procedures involving a break in atmosphere, skin and mucous membrane"},{"label":"D","text":"Surgical asepsis refers to practices that render and keep objects and areas free from micro-organisms"},{"label":"E","text":"Contamination is the process by which an instrument is soiled with micro organisms"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b9e79c93f17f","stem":"The following are examples of an acquired fistula except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fistula-in-ano"},{"label":"B","text":"Thyroglossal fistula"},{"label":"C","text":"Arteriovenous fistula"},{"label":"D","text":"Branchial fistula"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above are acquired fistulae"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c7399f4df2e3","stem":"The following is true about incarcerated hernia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Abdo