...................."},{"label":"A","text":"Active sites"},{"label":"B","text":"Catalytic sites"},{"label":"C","text":"Substrates"},{"label":"D","text":"Substrate binding sites Enzymes are stereo specific catalysts and typically catalyse reactions of only one stereoisomer of a given compound eg. ..................."},{"label":"A","text":"D-but not L sugars"},{"label":"B","text":"D and L sugars"},{"label":"C","text":"L-but not D Amino acids"},{"label":"D","text":"A and C The commonly used names of the enzymes describe the ......................"},{"label":"A","text":"Type of reaction"},{"label":"B","text":"Stereotype of the substrate"},{"label":"C","text":"Amount of substrate"},{"label":"D","text":"Discoverer Atomic rearrangements in configuration is mainly achieved by ......................."},{"label":"A","text":"Transferases"},{"label":"B","text":"Isomerases"},{"label":"C","text":"Reductases"},{"label":"D","text":"Decarboxylases Prosthetic groups, Cofactors and Coenzymes affect the catalytic capability of the enzymes by inducing the configuration of active site by binding on to ....................."},{"label":"A","text":"Hydrogen bonding"},{"label":"B","text":"Van de wall forces"},{"label":"C","text":"Aminoacyl side chains"},{"label":"D","text":"FAD Among the other, ........................... is one of the prosthetic groups which binds tightly to enzyme structure"},{"label":"A","text":"Biotin"},{"label":"B","text":"Vitamin A 8"},{"label":"C","text":"Metalloenzymes"},{"label":"D","text":"Metalloproteinase Ester compound can be catalysed by enzyme from of the following classes"},{"label":"A","text":"Esterase"},{"label":"B","text":"Hydrolases"},{"label":"C","text":"Decarboxylases"},{"label":"D","text":"Oxdoreductase Enzymes like Pyruvate decarboxylase is cosubstrated by ....................."},{"label":"A","text":"Niacin"},{"label":"B","text":"Mg2+"},{"label":"C","text":"TTP/TPP"},{"label":"D","text":"Biotin Mechanisms of enzymes catalytic activities are largely dependent on several factors including Enzyme-substrate bond strain and ..............................."},{"label":"A","text":"Proximity orientation"},{"label":"B","text":"Protein-protein interaction"},{"label":"C","text":"Hydrogen bonding"},{"label":"D","text":"Ester bond"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Medical Biochemistry","displayTopic":"Proteins and Enzymes","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_labels","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-b4d3c782e8fe","stem":"Which of the following statements about the urea cycle is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Argininosuccinate is lysed to urea and ornithine in the urea cycle. 20"},{"label":"B","text":"Carbamoyl phosphate supplies both of the nitrogen atoms of urea in the urea cycle."},{"label":"C","text":"The formation of urea from the urea cycle yields energy."},{"label":"D","text":"Arginine is hydrolysed to urea and ornithine in the urea cycle."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_un