gned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mention by use of a phrase of 2 to 5 words what knee apparatus has been injured"},{"label":"B","text":"List the components or levels of possible injury to this apparatus:"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Orthopedics","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["prior_structural_review_flag","requires_visual_review","topic_generic","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ab214bc06fa5","stem":"This question is about the brachial plexus Joe is a 40 year old watchman employed by the coffee factory in town. One day after night duty he found that his right wrist was weak and he could not extend it. He went to see a doctor. He told the doctor that he had had no injury or remarkable incident. He had slept while sitting on a chair his arm resting and hanging on the back of the chair. In relation to this case write down short answers to these questions: (A) What is the diagnosis?___________________________________________ (B) What important structure has been affected?__________________________ (C) Where is the anatomical position of this structure? (D) What is the treatment?___________________________________________","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e35215