ull-term male newborn is found to have a tuft of hair on the midline in | |the lumbar region. Palpation of the area shows an absence of spinous processes in that region. Imaging studies show no | |additional abnormalities. The most likely cause of this defect was failure of which of the following events during gestation?| | | | | |A | |. | |Development of the notochord | | | | | |B | |. | |Formation of the neural tube | | | | | |C | |. | |Formation of the yolk sac | | | | | |D | |. | |Fusion of the sclerotomes | | | | | |E | |. | |Migration of the neural crests | | |","type":"OSCE / Practical Station","subject":"Embryology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["prior_structural_review_flag","requires_visual_review","topic_generic","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0afa46257727","stem":"Identify the pointed structure in figure 3 below","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vertebral spine"},{"label":"B","text":"Lamina"},{"label":"C","text":"Pedicle"},{"label":"D","text":"Vertebral body"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_gene